## Authoritative case format

This case is the FIVE reference for four-stage handoffs and proof reporting. Rocq organizes `no_error`, `termination`, and `cbmc_recheck` as named problems. Each `problem/` holds its specification and report. Each numbered `attempts/` entry records the proof, actual outcome, model configuration, input hashes, evidence, and observed costs or a reference to the shared stage run. The three problem specifications are ready for new proof attempts. Cross-model obligations use the same `problem/` and `attempts/` structure in `relations/<name>/`.
